  "summary": "Several studies directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to the task of estimating agricultural yield. Gupta et al. (2024) [V0039] report the highest performance with an accuracy of 0.89 on the CellLife dataset. Fischer et al. (2023) [V0038] achieve an F1 score of 0.82 using the LedgerGuard dataset. Haddad et al. (2025) [V0040] evaluate the method on ToxiBench, reporting a test MAE of 0.61. El-Sayed et al. (2022) [V0037] apply the method to AgriSat-4, achieving an AUROC of 0.75. A related document [V0097] mentions this application as prior work but focuses on hate speech detection.",
